<h1>signature</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The types or <a href="domain.html"><em>domains</em></a>, and order, in some representations, of inputs to and outputs from a <a href="function.html"><em>function</em></a>.
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
For instance, the signature of the C library function <tt>strncmp()</tt> (compare up to n characters of two <a href="string.html"><em>strings</em></a>) is <tt>int (char *, char *, int)</tt>.  That is, it takes two C strings and an integer, and returns an integer.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPR">PR</a></p>

<hr>

